domain RepositionOriginalAreaId:
  description "Current offline canonical battlefield area identity mismatch"
problem P1:
  "One adjacent hop must preserve frozen battlefield topology and canonical area IDs."
evidence E1:
  |
    ADR0020 D1 bounds one accepted reposition to one adjacent topology hop.
    ADR0022 D1 separates canonical placement/topology from observer perception.
    The existing three-area fixture supplies area.1 sand, area.2 stone, area.3 center
    and frozen entryAreas a area.1 b area.3 with two topology edges.
evidence E2:
  |
    battle-engine.ts translates frozen entry IDs into initial semantic display names
    then calls createBattleWorldState with semanticState only. battle-world.ts
    buildAreaMapping sorts only labels present in semantic entities and generates
    new area.N IDs. Empty middle areas are not seeded from battlefield definitions.
evidence E3:
  |
    Strengthened regression in reposition-transition.test.ts asserts three original
    area IDs, canonical a area.1 and b area.3, then a single hop to area.2 rather
    than directly to the target. Current before-repair TAP fails missing area.3;
    other two cases pass. The former first case passed with generated IDs and an
    assertion that the hop reached the target, failing to verify the intended chain.
evidence E4:
  |
    A perception or provider failure cannot explain the initializer's absent middle
    canonical area: this isolated pure initialization has no provider calls.
    Historical introduction, existing battle repair policy and any production impact
    remain unknown. This result does not establish every canonical topology issue.
decision D1 based_on P1, E1, E2, E3, E4:
  |
    The current producing condition is losing frozen area identity and unoccupied
    areas while translating IDs to display labels and regenerating area.N IDs.
    Three declared areas trigger the mismatch. The generated-ID-based assertion
    explains this test's detection gap; historical detection failures are unknown.
decision D2 based_on D1, E1, E4:
  |
    Preserve supplied frozen area IDs and all declared areas during new battle
    initialization, and explicitly map entry IDs to canonical actor placements.
    Keep legacy callers without area definitions deterministic and preserve saved
    existing world state. Inspect duplicate display labels and source/schema limits
    before choosing the typed initialization contract. Do not rewrite old battles or
    declare this repair complete merely because the original weaker test passes.
